        "b_sci":  "Pterois volitans",
        "b_first":  "Native to Indian Ocean, Red Sea, and South Pacific, lionfish were likely aquarium releases, first seen off Florida in 1985. Larvae (young) ride currents through the Atlantic, Caribbean, and Gulf.",
        "b_path":  "Divers: photograph a lionfish from a safe distance and report it on the REEF form, which feeds USGS NAS. Never touch one. Its spines sting even when the fish is dead. Never release aquarium pets.",
        "b_impacts":  "In one Bahamas test, a single lionfish on a small reef cut new young fish by 79%. It gobbles native reef fish, has venomous spines, and almost nothing hunts it.",
