        "b_sci":  "Channa argus",
        "b_first":  "Native to China, Russia, and Korea. In 2002, someone dumped two snakeheads in a Maryland pond, and nearly 100 young appeared. Found in the Potomac River in 2004, they spread.",
        "b_path":  "Photograph a suspected snakehead safely and report it at USGS NAS \"Report a Sighting,\" with an adult. Never dump pet or market fish in any water; Crofton began with two. Anglers: know your state\u0027s release rules.",
