        "b_sci":  "Ictalurus furcatus",
        "b_first":  "Blue catfish are native to Mississippi, Missouri, Ohio, and Rio Grande basins. In the 1970s and 1980s, Virginia stocked them in tidal rivers for fishing. Outside that range, they are invasive.",
        "b_path":  "Spot one outside its home basins? Photograph it safely and report it at USGS NAS \"Report a Sighting,\" with an adult. Never move live fish between waters. Where states ask, keep and kill your catch.",
