        "b_sci":  "Ctenopharyngodon idella",
        "b_first":  "Native to eastern Asia, grass carp were imported in 1963 to eat weeds in streams, ponds and lakes. Some escaped, the first of the invasive carps. Stocking and releases spread them through Mississippi basin and into the Great Lakes.",
        "b_path":  "Photograph a grass carp safely and report it at USGS NAS \"Report a Sighting,\" with an adult. Anglers: never release one; freeze it, call your state fish and wildlife authorities. Ponds: certified triploid fish only (three chromosome sets, cannot reproduce).",
        "b_impacts":  "A broad-headed grass carp over 3 feet long can strip underwater plants that fish and ducks need. It also eats leaves and grasses that fall into the water.",
